      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "`tap`: The processing tap.",
      "contextAfter": "`processingFormat`: The format in which the client will receive the audio data to be processed. This will always be the same sample rate as the client format and usually the same number of channels as the client format of the audio queue. (NOTE: the number of channels may be different in some cases if the client format has some channel count restrictions; for example, if the client provides 5.1 AAC, but the decoder can only produce stereo). The channel order, if the same as the client format, will be the same as the client channel order. If the channel count is changed, it will be to either 1 (mono) or 2 (stereo, in which case the first channel is left, the second right). If the data is not in a convenient format for the client to process in, then the client should convert the data to and from that format. This is the most   efficient mechanism to use, as the audio system may choose a format that is most efficient from its playback requirement.",
      "documentTitle": "MTAudioProcessingTapPrepareCallback",
      "framework": "MediaToolbox",
      "meta": {
